  "misconception": {
    "title": "Constant speed read as 'free' energy",
    "detail": "Many learners treat 'holding 38 m/s' as neutral — it is not. Under conservation of mechanical energy, the kinetic-energy term ½v² is held fixed, so every metre of height must be spent purely against drag along the polar. The right move is to write the height ledger first (available Δh versus the altitude the polar charges for the remaining distance) before accepting any speed the pilot wants to hold."
  },
